{"base_rate":0.4367588932806324,"brier":0.23069229249011855,"bss":0.06222859728506813,"bss_hi":0.1822660561103658,"bss_lo":-0.0676623163769805,"chart":{"base":[628.3,212.2],"fp":[325.6,185.7],"lead":"62,239.8 272,214.2 482,167.2 692,123.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.06 — higher than 10% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +27pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 43% of cities","rel":"promised 7% → rained 18%; promised 97% → rained 67%"},"rel":"103.8,386.9 421.9,265 670.9,174.5"},"country":"LV","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.18480237154150198,"ess":343.72671961095267,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Riga</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Riga rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>72%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>12%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 506 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-02-09. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.06, ranked 121 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(110&ndash;129) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>147</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>49</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>54%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>87%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>47</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Riga</b> <span class=\"muted\">LV</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.06</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>110&ndash;129\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>506 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Riga &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Riga\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" fon